## height
# HEIGHT. Every cell is authored so the smoothing pass cannot build a staircase up the side of
# anything here. '0' is the town floor; a voxel is HALF a walk cell, so '2' is one cell up and '4'
# is two. Walking climbs one voxel free, so a '2' beside a '0' already needs a hop and a '4' beside
# a '0' cannot be climbed at all (the jump apex is 2.5 voxels). Every raised block is TERRAIN with
# paving under it, never a stamp: a stamp is solid and its top is not walkable.
#
# THE BELL RUN (chapter01.md P5). The party arrives at 31,2 and wants the guild-hall counter at
# 34-35,20. The counter stands in the guild CLOSE, which the hedge at z16 and the hall itself seal
# from the north and the close wall at x28 seals from the square. On foot the only way in is the
# long one: down the lane, round the square, south past the lamp to z29, east under the back wall,
# in at the grain yard's propped door (x34, z29-31), through the yard and out of the gap in its far
# wall at 40-41,26. That is 67 cells of walking (measured on the nav dump) and it does not make it.
#
# Three shortcuts, all of them jumps, in the order the chapter teaches them. The engine turns a
# lone two-voxel step with level ground opposite into a RAMP (vx_build, step 4), which is why the
# '2' blocks — the step, the kerb, the trough — can be walked up: they are the run-up, and every
# '4' above them still has to be jumped for.
#
#   1. THE ROOFS OFF THE LANE.  step 24,12 ('2') -> roof1 x25-27 z11-13 ('4', the house whose stamp
#      was removed) -> roof2 x30-31 z11-13 ('4') -> a two-cell drop south into the alley behind the
#      hall at 29-30,14.  The gap between the roofs is x28-x29 at z11-13: TWO empty cells, so the
#      body leaves x=27.76 and must land at x>=30.24 -> 2.48 cells of travel. A running jump carries
#      3.6 and a walking one 2.2, so the run clears it and the walk does not. From the alley the
#      counter is fourteen cells away: 17 + 7 + 14 = 38 cells against the direct route's 67.
#
#   2. OVER THE GRAIN-YARD WALL.  trough x32-33 z27 ('2') -> the back wall z26 ('4') -> run east
#      along it and drop north into the close, or east over the gate gap and down into the yard.
#      Ground to trough is 2 voxels (a hop), trough to wall another 2; from the ground the wall's 4
#      voxels are unclimbable. The gate gap at x40-41 is again TWO empty cells of wall top: 2.48
#      cells, run-only, exactly as above. 43 + 10 + 8 = 61 against 67 — six cells, and it also
#      skips the three {{GRAIN_CREATURE_PL}} on the yard route, which is where its time goes.
#
#   3. THE WELL KERB TO THE LOW SHED — the small one, for players who missed the other two.
#      kerb x23-24 z19-20 ('2', beside the well) -> ONE empty cell at x25 -> the shed roof
#      x26-27 z19-20 ('4') -> walk straight onto the close wall at x28 and drop into the alley.
#      1 + 0.48 = 1.48 cells of travel with a one-cell rise: at walking speed the body is still
#      2.2 voxels up when it lands, so even a standing jump makes it. Forgiving on purpose.
#      26 + 7 + 7 = 40 against 67.
#
# If VX_SP_RUN, VX_SP_WALK, VX_JUMP_APEX, VX_GRAVITY or VX_AGENT_R changes in voxfield.cpp, the two
# 2.48-cell gaps have to be re-measured.
